Hi :) I am working on a salamander morphology project and have very little experience working with computer software and coding. Using tpsUtil32, we converted our images to TPS files, appended the files into a master TPS file, and then plotted 12 landmarks on each image in tpsDig232. Then we entered these commands in Geomorph:

readland.tps(file.choose())

MyShapeData_tps=readland.tps(
fixed.angle(myShapeData_tps,art.pt <http://art.pt/>=1,angle.pts=c(5,6),rot.pts=c(2,3,4,5))
myData.super <- gpagen(myShapeData_tps)
plotTangentSpace(fixed.angle(myShapeData_tps,art.pt <http://art.pt/>=1,angle.pts=c(5,6),rot.pts=c(2,3,4,5)))

Our main question is: how do you correctly code for superimposition? We attempted entering myData.super <- gpagen(myShapeData_tps) but this consistently seemed to do nothing. A line appeared on the screen labeled 100%, but our resulting plot looked the same regardless of whether we used the command or not. We appreciate any help you can provide!

Thanks,

Brittany

