Yes, QuaSSE is for quantitative traits. An alternative, which ought to be adaptable to multidimensional data is in Harvey, M. G., D. L. Rabosky, and N. Cooper. 2018. Continuous traits and speciation rates: Alternatives to state-dependent diversification models. Methods Ecol. Evol. 9:984-993. This uses either PGLS or simulations to test for a relationship between tip-specific speciation rates and trait evolution. The problem is that you need a model for trait evolution (whether you use PGLS or simulations given parameters of the model).

