I apologize for not being clearer. The overall appearance of the graph is as expected and consistent with the various tests I ran. What seems 'off' is that the trajectories themselves (which just connect neighboring ontogenetic stages) are each offset from the clouds of points for their respective species. In other words, I'd expect the trajectories to be more-or-less centered within the distribution for each species, but they are not. When I generate a comparable plot elsewhere (in SAS), the centroids for each stage and the resulting low-dimensional projections of the trajectories are centered within the respective distributions.

I think this is perhaps related to centering that is done for the plotting? But that's just my guess.

I hope this is clearer...

